          `**What if sahi word yaad na aaye?** Tab roots se banao. Definition hai "one who knows everything" — root yaad karo: "omni" (all) + "scient" (knowing) = "omniscient". Definition hai "one who loves mankind" — "phile" (lover) + "anthropo" (mankind) = "philanthropist". Root method se aap bhoola hua word bhi wapas bana sakte ho. Aur agar root bhi yaad na aaye, toh options ke roots dekho: kaunsa option definition ke key word se match karta hai?

**What if saare options naye hon?** Tab elimination use karo. Definition hai "a place where bees are kept". Options hain: (a) aviary (b) apiary (c) mortuary (d) library. "Mortuary" mein dead bodies hoti hain — hatao. "Library" mein books hoti hain — hatao. Ab bache "aviary" aur "apiary". "Avi" = bird, "api" = bee. Definition mein "bees" hai, isliye jawab hai "apiary". Elimination se chaar options do reh gaye, aur root se final jawab mil gaya. Yeh combination — elimination + root — exam mein sabse strong strategy hai.

**What if definition bahut lambi ho?** Lambi definition mein key words dhoondho — aksar sirf 2-3 words matter karte hain. Jaise "a person who is fond of the company of others and likes to talk to people" — key words hain "company of others" aur "likes to talk". Matlab hai social insaan — jawab hai "extrovert" ya "gregarious". Lambi definition se ghabrayein nahi; use chhota karke padho — sirf key words par dhyaan do.`,
          `**What if you cannot remember the right word?** Then build it from the roots. The definition is "one who knows everything" — remember the roots: "omni" (all) + "scient" (knowing) = "omniscient". The definition is "one who loves mankind" — "phile" (lover) + "anthropo" (mankind) = "philanthropist". With the root method you can rebuild even a forgotten word. And if you cannot remember the root either, look at the roots of the options: which option matches the key word of the definition?

**What if all the options are new?** Then use elimination. The definition is "a place where bees are kept". The options are: (a) aviary (b) apiary (c) mortuary (d) library. A "mortuary" holds dead bodies — remove it. A "library" holds books — remove it. Now "aviary" and "apiary" remain. "Avi" = bird, "api" = bee. The definition says "bees", so the answer is "apiary". Elimination reduced four options to two, and the root gave the final answer. This combination — elimination plus root — is the strongest strategy in an exam.

**What if the definition is very long?** In a long definition, find the key words — often only 2 or 3 words matter. For example, "a person who is fond of the company of others and likes to talk to people" — the key words are "company of others" and "likes to talk". The meaning is a social person — the answer is "extrovert" or "gregarious". Do not fear a long definition; shorten it as you read it — focus only on the key words.`
