          `**Galti 1: Bina subject ke email bhejna.** Bina subject wala email spam jaisa lagta hai aur log use kholte hi nahi. Subject mein hamesha purpose aur date likho. "Hello" ya "Important" subject nahi hote — woh kuch batate hi nahi. Achhi subject hoti hai "Request for leave on 20 November" ya "Report for the sales meeting".

**Galti 2: Informal language use karna.** Email mein "Hey", "Whats up", "u" aur "plz" mat likho. Yeh chat ki language hai, business ki nahi. Formal email mein "Dear Sir", "I would like to", aur "Thank you" use karo. Ek informal word bhi email ko unprofessional bana sakta hai.

**Galti 3: Bahut lamba email likhna.** Agar email mein 5 paragraphs hain aur har paragraph 6 lines ka hai, toh koi use poora nahi padhega. Email ko 150 words se kam rakho. Lambi baat hai toh points mein likho ya attachment bhejo. Chhota email zyada padha jaata hai.

**Galti 4: Gusse mein email bhejna.** Gusse mein likha email aksar regret ka reason banta hai. Agar gussa aa raha ho, toh email likh kar draft mein rakho aur 10 minute baad phir padho. Polite words se baat zyada jaldi solve hoti hai.`,
          `**Mistake 1: Sending an email without a subject.** An email without a subject looks like spam, and people do not even open it. Always write the purpose and the date in the subject. "Hello" or "Important" are not subjects — they say nothing. A good subject is "Request for leave on 20 November" or "Report for the sales meeting".

**Mistake 2: Using informal language.** Do not write "Hey", "Whats up", "u", or "plz" in an email. That is chat language, not business language. In a formal email, use "Dear Sir", "I would like to", and "Thank you". Even one informal word can make an email look unprofessional.

**Mistake 3: Writing a very long email.** If an email has 5 paragraphs and each paragraph is 6 lines long, nobody will read it fully. Keep an email under 150 words. If the message is long, write it in points or send an attachment. A short email is read more often.

**Mistake 4: Sending an email in anger.** An email written in anger often becomes a regret. If you feel angry, write the email, save it as a draft, and read it again after 10 minutes. Polite words solve a problem faster.`
