          `**Mistake 1: Copying the sentences of the passage.** A précis must be written in your own words. If you join the sentences of the passage to make a précis, that is not a précis, it is copy-paste. The examiner catches this at once and cuts marks. First understand the passage, then close it and write in your own words.

**Mistake 2: Adding your own opinion.** A précis never has "I think" or "In my opinion". You are only shortening what the writer said, not giving your view. If the passage says water must be saved, write the same in the précis — do not add from your side that "saving water is very hard".

**Mistake 3: Keeping examples and details.** Examples do not belong in a précis. The passage had examples of taps and cars, but they should not appear in the précis. Keep only the main points. If you keep the examples, the précis becomes long and breaks the one-third rule.

**Mistake 4: Changing the main idea.** Sometimes a student makes a small detail the main idea of the précis. For example, making car washing the main idea of the water passage is wrong — the main idea is saving water. Always ask: what point is the writer stressing the most?`
