          `**What if words zyada ho jaayein?** Har sentence ko chhota karo. "People use water for drinking, cooking, and farming" ko "People need water for daily use" likho. Adjectives aur extra words hatao. Har sentence mein sirf main point rakho. Agar phir bhi zyada hon, toh sabse kam important point ko hata do.

**What if apne words na milein?** Passage ke mushkil words ke simple synonyms dhoondho. "Essential" ki jagah "needed" likho, "waste" ki jagah "lose" likho. Simple words se précis bhi saaf hota hai aur aapke words bhi apne lagte hain. Dictionary wale mushkil words ki zaroorat nahi hai.

**What if main idea samajh na aaye?** Passage ke pehle aur aakhri sentence ko padho — main idea aksar wahi hota hai. Pehla sentence topic batata hai aur aakhri sentence conclusion batata hai. Beech ke paragraphs sirf details hote hain. Yeh trick mushkil passage mein bahut kaam aati hai.

**What if time kam ho?** Pehle main points ko rough mein likho, phir unko jod kar précis likho. Rough points likhne mein 3 minute lagte hain, par usse précis 10 minute mein likha jaata hai. Bina points ke seedha précis likhna aksar lamba aur bhatka hua hota hai.`,
          `**What if the words go over the limit?** Shorten every sentence. Write "People need water for daily use" instead of "People use water for drinking, cooking, and farming". Remove adjectives and extra words. Keep only the main point in each sentence. If the words are still too many, remove the least important point.

**What if you cannot find your own words?** Find simple synonyms for the hard words of the passage. Write "needed" instead of "essential" and "lose" instead of "waste". Simple words make the précis clear and make the words feel like your own. There is no need for difficult dictionary words.

**What if you cannot understand the main idea?** Read the first and the last sentence of the passage — the main idea is often there. The first sentence states the topic and the last sentence states the conclusion. The middle paragraphs hold only details. This trick helps a lot with a hard passage.

**What if time is short?** First write the main points in rough, then join them into a précis. Writing rough points takes 3 minutes, but it lets you write the précis in 10 minutes. Writing a précis directly without points often makes it long and scattered.`
