        body: t(
          `Summarizing ka matlab hai ek lambe passage ko chhota karke uski main baat likhna. Summary mein passage ka **main idea** hota hai — woh ek baat jo poora passage keh raha hai — aur **key points** hote hain — woh 2 ya 3 points jo main idea ko support karte hain. Examples, numbers aur extra details summary mein nahi aate. Summary apne words mein likha jaata hai.

Summary aur précis mein farak hai. Précis mein one-third rule follow karna hota hai aur passage ka order bhi follow karna hota hai. Summary mein aapko zyada freedom hoti hai — aap points ko apne order mein likh sakte ho aur length bhi thodi upar-neeche ho sakti hai. Exam mein summary aksar 5 se 8 lines mein maanga jaata hai, chahe passage kitna bhi lamba ho.

Summary likhne ke liye passage ko samajhna zaroori hai. Agar aap passage ko samjhe bina summary likhoge, toh aap galat points likh doge. Isliye pehle passage ko do baar padho, phir main idea ek line mein likho, aur phir key points ko jod do. Summary mein aapki apni opinion nahi hoti — sirf passage ki baat hoti hai.`,
          `Summarizing means shortening a long passage to its main message. A summary holds the **main idea** of the passage — the one point the whole passage makes — and the **key points** — the 2 or 3 points that support the main idea. Examples, numbers, and extra details do not belong in a summary. A summary is written in your own words.

A summary and a précis are different. A précis must follow the one-third rule and the order of the passage. A summary gives you more freedom — you may write the points in your own order, and the length may vary a little. In exams, a summary is often asked in 5 to 8 lines, however long the passage is.

To write a summary, you must understand the passage. If you write a summary without understanding the passage, you will write the wrong points. So first read the passage twice, then write the main idea in one line, and then add the key points. A summary holds no opinion of your own — only what the passage says.`
        )
