          `**Speed reading** ka matlab hai tez padhna — bina samajh khoye. Iski speed ko **WPM** se naapte hain, jiska matlab hai **words per minute**, yaani ek minute mein kitne words padhe. Aam aadmi lagbhag **200 WPM** ki speed se padhta hai. Achha reader **300-400 WPM** tak padh sakta hai. Exam mein speed reading ka fayda yeh hai ki lamba passage jaldi padh kar questions ke liye zyada time bach jaata hai.

Speed reading ka matlab sirf tez-tez aankhein ghumana nahi hai. Agar aap tez padho par kuch samajh na aaye, toh woh speed reading nahi hai, woh sirf page palatna hai. Asli speed reading mein **speed aur samajh dono** badhte hain. Iske liye teen cheezein chahiye: pehle, **skimming** — passage ko jaldi se dekh kar main idea samajhna. Doosra, **scanning** — kisi khaas jaankari ko dhoondhna, jaise date ya naam. Teesra, **focus** — ek baar mein poora passage padhna, bina peeche mudhe.

Is article mein hum WPM nikaalna seekhenge, skimming aur scanning ka farak samjhenge, aur do badi galtiyon — sub-vocalization aur regression — ko rokna seekhenge. Aakhir mein aap apni reading speed ko khud naap paayenge.`,
          `**Speed reading** means reading fast — without losing understanding. Its speed is measured in **WPM**, which means **words per minute**, or how many words you read in one minute. An average person reads at about **200 WPM**. A good reader can reach **300-400 WPM**. The benefit of speed reading in an exam is that you finish a long passage quickly and save more time for the questions.

Speed reading does not mean just moving your eyes fast. If you read fast but understand nothing, that is not speed reading — that is only turning pages. In real speed reading, **both speed and understanding** grow. It needs three things: first, **skimming** — looking at a passage quickly to grasp the main idea. Second, **scanning** — searching for a specific piece of information, like a date or a name. Third, **focus** — reading the whole passage in one go, without going back.

In this article we will learn how to work out WPM, understand the difference between skimming and scanning, and stop two big mistakes — sub-vocalization and regression. By the end, you will be able to measure your own reading speed.`
